  "question": {
    "text": "<p><strong>Assertion A:</strong> Product of Pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>P</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> has the same dimension as that of coefficient of viscosity.</p><p><strong>Reason:</strong> Coefficient of viscosity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Force</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Velocity</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gradient</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cvVeR",
      "text": "Both A&nbsp;and R&nbsp;true, and R&nbsp;is correct explanation of A.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oZJZx",
      "text": "Both A&nbsp;and R&nbsp;are true but R&nbsp;is NOT the correct explanation of A.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nalfo",
      "text": "A is true but R&nbsp;is false.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "WLsFF",
      "text": "A is false but R&nbsp;is true.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Viscous force is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#951;</mi><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is area and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is velocity gradient.</p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mi>A</mi></mfrac><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#951;</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#951;</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Thus, assertion is true but reason is false.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
